PART C  --  CONSERVATIVE threshold C(k)=c*k (c=1) via upward-closure prune
==============================================================================
  RIGOROUS PRUNE: p_0 is upward-closed (E1 subset E2 => p_0(E1) <= p_0(E2)).
  For prefix P with future window W, every completion C in [P, P u W] obeys
  p_0(C) <= p_0(P u W); if that bound <= cap_k the whole subtree is certified.
  Scale-invariance restricts to primitive E.

